Apple Inc. (AAPL) Chief Executive Tim Cook will be deposed on June 27, as part of Qualcomm Inc.'s (QCOM) lawsuit against the iPhone maker, according to court documents. Apple stock is down 1.4% in after-hours trading and closed up less than 1% to $172.80. The suit accuses Apple of misleading regulators in order to generate investigations into Qualcomm. The lawsuit filed in the Southern California district court is a part of a larger legal fight between Apple and Qualcomm, which began last year and revolves around chip royalties Apple paid to Qualcomm. Apple stock is up 2.1% this year, as the S&P 500 index has lost less than 1%.
-Max A. Cherney;
 05-18 1923ET
